d him it was clear to Wakaba that  Sonic's proportions had to change so you  could see his body more clearly his  quills became sharper and doubled in  size his nose arms and legs got longer  overall he became more angular and less  round and he lost his potbelly Sonic  smooth blue fur became a darker shade of  blue and his eyes became green to  contrast with his skin hue Kawa cites  Akira Toriyama's line calligraphy as his  influence Toriyama is famous for having  created two characters for Dragon Ball Z  and is the reason this new Sonic looked  as why Kawa has said more graffiti or  street like Sonic was no longer cute he  was cool to double down on this new  Western coolness Sonic Adventure 2 in  2001 gave sonic shoes that looked more  like American sneakers much like the old  version of Sonic this new version was  featured in peripheral TV shows and  comics Sonic games since then haven't  delineated too much on his design in  2006 however Yuji naka wanted to create  a Sonic game with the more realistic  tone the game simply called Sonic the  Hedgehog reintroduced the concept of  another human love interest for Sonic  Elyse is a princess who has a secret  power that dr. Eggman wants to exploit  Sonic saves her time and time again  because Sonic had to interact with the  lease of full-sized human they made him  slightly taller and more mature  [Music]  nice smile  that game let alone that relationship  was seen as a huge failure and prompted  Sega to return to a lighter tone for  Sonic games a 2008 game called Sonic  Unleashed introduced a werehog version  of Sonic in which she became furry and  muscular in the sonic boom franchise  launched in 2014 to make Sonic look more  like what audiences recognize in a hero  art director Bob ruff a gave him  bandages tattered hair and a scarf this  design gave us another radical deviation  from the traditional Sonic design and  that this version had blue arms instead  of flesh colored ones this franchise is  seen as an outlier in terms of Sonic's  appearance though as the modern Sonic is  still being used in other games and  media that leads us to Sonic the  Hedgehog the film produced by Paramount  Pictures  initially the designers for the film  created a sonic that was supposed to  resemble a realistic Hedgehog the eyes  were small he had creepy human-like  teeth and generally looks like a small  child in a onesie it was a disaster  Sonic fans hated the design so much that  director Jeff Fowler promised he would  change it to better reflect Sega's  modern version of Sonic paramount  released a new updated trailer in early  2020 the revamped sonic looks much  better but there are still a few  differences the biggest one is his eyes  paramount version of Sonic has two  eyeballs  whereas Sega's version famously only has  one with two pupils his arms are blue  like the sonic boom version and the new  design also fades Sonic's new fur into  his tan mouth for a slightly more  realistic depiction in the movie he has  noticeable firm versus the smooth skin  on Sega's version of Sonic paramount  also gave its Sonic's some cool new  sneakers similar to the one seen in  Sonic Adventure 2 overall Paramount's  version seems to be a combination of all  the Sonic's we've seen thus far while  sticking  to the 90s a stetic sonic has come a  long way from Teddy Roosevelt and  rabbits to the live-action form we see  today but the latest backlash just goes  to show that fans prefer the Sonic they  grew up with in the 90s and that change  isn't always a good thing  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

